<ArticleLayout slug="how-to-become-permanent-resident-canada" datePublished="2026-10-18" dateModified="2026-10-18" articleSection="Guide" keywords="how to become a permanent resident in Canada, how do I become a PR in Canada, how to get Canadian PR, Canada permanent residency 2026, how to apply for Canada permanent residence, how to get PR from inside Canada, Express Entry, Provincial Nominee Program, Canadian PR requirements" title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <div class="inline-block bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-800 px-4 py-1 rounded-full text-sm font-bold mb-4 border border-indigo-200 shadow-sm">
        PR Pillar Guide
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
        How to Become a Permanent Resident in Canada (2026): Every Way to Get Canadian PR
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-4">
        Every federal and provincial route to Canadian permanent residence, checked against official sources in October 2026, including the programs that are paused and the Express Entry points changes coming on November 3.
      </p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <time datetime="2026-10-18">October 18, 2026</time>
        <span>&bull;</span>
        <span>16 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-indigo-50 border-2 border-indigo-200 p-6 rounded-2xl mb-10">
