      <p class="text-indigo-900">
        To become a permanent resident in Canada, you must qualify under one immigration program, apply to Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada (IRCC), pass medical, criminal and security checks, and then land in Canada. Most skilled workers get PR through <strong>Express Entry</strong> or a <strong>Provincial Nominee Program</strong>; others qualify through Quebec's own selection, the Atlantic Immigration Program, a rural or francophone community pilot, or sponsorship by a Canadian spouse or partner. As of October 2026, the caregiver, parent and grandparent, and start-up visa routes are not accepting new applications.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
      <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 rounded-2xl text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-black text-indigo-600 mb-2">380,000</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-slate-600 font-medium">Federal PR admissions target for 2026</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 rounded-2xl text-center">
