            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Outside Canada, no job offer</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Express Entry FSW; French category if you reach NCLC 7; provincial Express Entry streams that do not need an offer</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Proof of funds; general CRS cutoffs have been well above 500</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Temporary worker in Canada</td><td class="px-4 py-3">CEC; your province's worker stream; AIP or RCIP/FCIP if your employer is designated</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Work permit expiry; only skilled (TEER 0–3) work counts for CEC</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">International graduate</td><td class="px-4 py-3">CEC after a year of skilled work; provincial streams that award points for local study</td><td class="px-4 py-3">B.C. and Ontario no longer run graduate-only streams; work during studies generally doesn't count for CEC</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Tradesperson</td><td class="px-4 py-3">FST; Express Entry trades rounds; provincial trades priorities such as B.C.'s Build draws</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Provinces often require a Canadian trade certificate</td></tr>
